@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:concurrency] compute-host-capacity-serialization
Admission, restart reservations, accepted host reports, credential/session changes,
physical outcomes and maintenance transitions MUST serialize on the host row in
the shared database. When VM rows are also locked, host locks MUST precede VM
locks; a VM-locked callback MUST NOT acquire its host lock afterward.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] compute-trusted-coordinator-entry
Ledger mutations and operator enrollment, credential and maintenance helpers MUST
remain trusted in-process interfaces. User requests MUST enter authorized Ash
actions; provisioner requests MUST authenticate credentials and fence their current
session before reaching host report or physical outcome mutation.

Administrator evacuation requests, controls, downtime approvals and replans MUST
write a redacted append-only audit event in the same transaction as the durable
campaign/item mutation; audit rows MUST contain only actor, target and action kind.

Administrator host admission and CPU/RAM margin changes MUST use the serialized
host action, require fresh readiness before enabling admission, and write the
same redacted audit shape; physical capacity limits remain deployment-owned.

Administrator lifecycle and relocation requests MUST append only actor, target and
action kind to the redacted audit log inside the same transaction as their durable
operation or relocation reservation. Idempotent replays MUST NOT create duplicate
audit rows.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:product] compute-retained-placement
Ordinary lifecycle transitions MUST retain the VM's owner, current placement,
immutable image, network profile and requested shape outside explicit ADR-0051 resize. Stop and start MUST retain
disk and address allocations. Resume capacity fallback MUST use the durable
checkpoint relocation coordinator, preserving RAM rather than rebooting. Only the
serialized relocation coordinator may change current placement and epoch,
while preserving workload identity, image, shape, sharing and address. The
ADR-0051 resize coordinator alone may change shape after matching physical evidence;
its unfinished request MUST exclude lifecycle, relocation and maintenance.
